    {
      "id": "9e795ez",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.3 Revenue Administration"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Tamil Nadu is divided into Revenue Divisions, Taluks, and Revenue Villages for administrative purposes. The District Collector heads each district and is the representative of the state government. Specific administrative hierarchy:",
      "id": "zhyhssf"
    },
    {
      "id": "bjle9r7",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "State → Districts (38) → Revenue Divisions → Taluks → Firkas → Revenue Villages",
        "District Collector: IAS officer; chief executive of district",
        "Revenue Divisional Officer (RDO): Sub-district level",
        "Tehsildar / Taluk Tahsildar: Taluk level; land records, revenue",
        "Village Administrative Officer (VAO): Village level (formerly Karnam)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "19tiwo1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.4 Tamil Nadu Public Service Commission (TNPSC)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The Tamil Nadu Public Service Commission (TNPSC) is a constitutional body established under Article 315 of the Indian Constitution. It recruits candidates for various state government services. Key TNPSC examinations include:",
      "id": "ritzujd"
